From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ep9
Subject: [PATCH] Store the strings of each property of strings in one flat
 table

The tables of the properties of strings (Basic_Emoji, the RGI emoji
sequences and RGI_Emoji, used by \p{...} with the v flag) were arrays of
slices: one pointer per string, 7,907 pointers in all. Each pointer is a
load-time relocation (a dyld fixup on macOS), paid by every program that
links regress, at every start, used or not.

Each table is now two integer arrays, the code points of all strings and
the end of each string (StringSetTable), with two pointers per table.
The parser reads the strings through StringSetTable::iter. gen-unicode
writes the new form; the strings and their order do not change.
---
 gen-unicode/src/main.rs              |     1 +
 gen-unicode/src/string_properties.rs |    28 +-
 src/parse.rs                         |     4 +-
 src/unicode.rs                       |    54 +-
 src/unicodetables.rs                 | 10919 ++++++-------------------
 tests/string_properties.rs           |    63 +
 6 files changed, 2741 insertions(+), 8328 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/string_properties.rs

